From 5b16f7e93c289d94c513c546276647268cf9a510 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SovereignOS Build <build@sovereignos.local>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:26:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] datamap: give every contacted address a server place
 (ADR-161)

The collector hands the first address of a lookup or connect to the service, which looks it up in the mapped ipmap.bin on the service thread and keeps only the country, the city, the ASN and the operator of the server, never the address. The place says where the server lies in the data, not where the company is based. The history keeps it only when the user chose so (HistoryCodec rows of seventeen fields, UserSettings.serverHistory, IDataMapService.setServerHistory at the end of the transaction order). The Binder entry gains seven fields and the snapshot one.
